      "sourceTextSha256": "f2f3ce8c8eeb4243c763927281772bf70b7b9c06edfbb907a28098a3d8c14be8",
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on a sightseeing tour of Mexico City’s historic centre.\n\nThe main stop is the Zócalo, one of the largest city squares, surrounded by important landmarks. These include the Metropolitan Cathedral, which features Spanish colonial architecture, and the National Palace.\n\nContinue on foot along Madero Street to the Casa de los Azulejos (House of Tiles), with its blue-and-white Talavera tile façade. The next stop is the Palacio de Bellas Artes (Palace of Fine Arts), an Art Nouveau and Art Deco building that hosts concerts, ballet performances and exhibitions.\n\nIn the afternoon, visit the National Museum of Anthropology. Its collections cover the archaeology, ethnography and art of Mexico’s Indigenous cultures.\n\nReturn to the hotel in the evening for an overnight stay.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-986f3332f46d53ddb5737edd",
        "model": "Codex GPT-6"
      }
